1
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,920
This town will be mine.

2
00:00:14,466 --> 00:00:15,160
All mine.

3
00:00:20,756 --> 00:00:22,100
It's a trap.

4
00:00:40,603 --> 00:00:41,853
I found the person you're looking for.

5
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:43,860
I found her.

6
00:01:21,593 --> 00:01:22,503
Singh!

7
00:01:23,110 --> 00:01:24,740
Singh, help!

8
00:02:46,643 --> 00:02:48,180
Please let Foon stay here,
Monk Teacher.

9
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:51,076
So no one can do harm to her.

10
00:03:02,096 --> 00:03:03,393
If Sergeant Toon comes
asking for information,

11
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,170
please handle it, sir.

12
00:03:06,130 --> 00:03:06,503
Mm-hmm.

13
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:16,656
Singh.

14
00:03:18,253 --> 00:03:18,813
And you...

15
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:19,796
Are you okay?

16
00:03:21,143 --> 00:03:22,733
You've made it to this day, Singh.

17
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:26,093
The day you must learn
the art of magic to protect yourself.

18
00:03:27,890 --> 00:03:28,936
If they already know...

19
00:03:29,853 --> 00:03:30,903
Have you already decided?

20
00:03:31,513 --> 00:03:34,223
Are you ready to cross the line from
white magic to black magic?

21
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,543
One day, you'll understand on your own.

22
00:03:41,633 --> 00:03:42,600
But if you want to know now,

23
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:45,606
try closing your eyes and meditating.

24
00:03:47,346 --> 00:03:48,656
What do you see in the darkness?

25
00:03:51,446 --> 00:03:54,376
Let your mind stay in the center,
between life and death.

26
00:04:33,713 --> 00:04:34,580
Is your heart...

27
00:04:35,426 --> 00:04:37,146
hot and trembling?

28
00:04:38,310 --> 00:04:39,933
That's how it is at first.

29
00:04:40,150 --> 00:04:42,430
But once you learn to control it,
it gets better.

30
00:04:45,413 --> 00:04:46,320
Your father was the same.

31
00:04:49,036 --> 00:04:50,450
Wanted to win at first.

32
00:04:52,103 --> 00:04:54,000
Thought he was smarter than others.

33
00:04:57,570 --> 00:04:58,760
But in the end,
it was just his own thinking.

34
00:05:00,113 --> 00:05:01,426
He wasn't that smart at all.

35
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,350
When he couldn't beg for anything...

36
00:05:08,903 --> 00:05:10,226
he turned to black magic.

37
00:05:14,746 --> 00:05:15,640
You're no different.

38
00:05:21,506 --> 00:05:22,773
I'm not like you.

39
00:05:23,673 --> 00:05:25,420
So what did you do this for? Huh?

40
00:05:26,833 --> 00:05:27,453
Yes.

41
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:31,306
Think carefully.
Society doesn't accept you.

42
00:05:31,583 --> 00:05:33,743
You're in the dark side of society.

43
00:05:33,970 --> 00:05:34,853
To be honest,

44
00:05:35,066 --> 00:05:36,853
you're a loser until you die.

45
00:05:37,470 --> 00:05:38,823
A loser until you die.

46
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:42,463
Let me tell you.

47
00:05:43,773 --> 00:05:44,816
Come serve under me.

48
00:05:45,933 --> 00:05:46,873
No rules.

49
00:05:47,333 --> 00:05:48,456
You don't need to rely on...

50
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:50,030
these losers.

51
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,096
Seriously.

52
00:05:54,510 --> 00:05:56,383
You can't define me.

53
00:05:57,653 --> 00:05:58,090
Hey.

54
00:05:59,850 --> 00:06:01,860
I'm talking to you nicely here.

55
00:06:02,946 --> 00:06:04,613
I'm making you an offer.

56
00:06:06,716 --> 00:06:07,863
That's your problem, fucker!

57
00:06:29,106 --> 00:06:30,280
Damn.

58
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,420
Just like your father, huh?

59
00:06:45,086 --> 00:06:47,670
I curse you!

60
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:58,213
It becomes a worldly matter now.

61
00:06:59,666 --> 00:07:01,070
I truly cannot get involved.

62
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,410
But I'll do what I can.

63
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:15,163
When studying magic discipline
to a certain point,

64
00:07:16,090 --> 00:07:17,670
there will be people who
want to test their skills.

65
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,483
They will try to protect themselves.

66
00:07:24,003 --> 00:07:25,363
Dark spells lie in wait.

67
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:28,026
Those who dwell on revenge,

68
00:07:28,733 --> 00:07:29,746
their minds will be weak.

69
00:07:30,373 --> 00:07:31,580
Entities can enter them.

70
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:35,916
They will go mad.

71
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,420
And fall into the world of dark arts.

72
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:41,713
Is there a way to remove the dark soul?

73
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:46,500
It depends on how powerful
the person who cast the spell on them is.

74
00:07:46,546 --> 00:07:47,670
How potent their magic is.

75
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:13,400
Itipi so. Visesei isese.

76
00:08:16,350 --> 00:08:17,896
Amen.

77
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,860
Which way you come, go that way!

78
00:09:19,043 --> 00:09:19,583
Come in.

79
00:09:20,853 --> 00:09:21,620
Inspector.

80
00:09:21,696 --> 00:09:22,943
I have some questions.

81
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:31,180
Singh.

82
00:09:31,463 --> 00:09:32,753
Or Singha Unchanam.

83
00:09:34,226 --> 00:09:36,586
He uses the same last name as
his mother, Mrs. Phim Unchanam.

84
00:09:37,373 --> 00:09:40,176
Singh's father's name is Itthi Nakwiwat.

85
00:09:41,310 --> 00:09:44,110
The same last name as
Inspector Chan Nakwiwat.

86
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:47,173
Itthi and you are brothers.

87
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:49,123
Singh is your own nephew.

88
00:09:49,736 --> 00:09:51,420
But you never mention him.

89
00:09:52,930 --> 00:09:54,663
You even seem to be keeping it a secret.

90
00:09:55,566 --> 00:09:56,626
What does that mean?

91
00:10:08,073 --> 00:10:09,963
That day, Itt went to Dan Chang.

92
00:10:10,936 --> 00:10:12,190
To arrest the Nakhon Sawan Tiger.

93
00:10:14,173 --> 00:10:17,276
The villagers knew well that
he was into black magic and sorcery.

94
00:10:18,536 --> 00:10:19,973
He had threatened before...

95
00:10:20,926 --> 00:10:23,056
to kill every family member involved.

96
00:10:24,170 --> 00:10:24,950
But you knew...

97
00:10:26,076 --> 00:10:28,020
that I wrote the report
based on what I saw.

98
00:10:28,793 --> 00:10:29,840
The Hem gang...

99
00:10:30,736 --> 00:10:31,760
the villagers also knew...

100
00:10:31,853 --> 00:10:33,263
that they couldn't be hurt
by blades or bullets.

101
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:35,256
They were practitioners of dark arts.

102
00:10:37,380 --> 00:10:38,633
Who would believe that?

103
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:41,976
The entire police department...

104
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:44,130
how many would believe it?

105
00:10:46,836 --> 00:10:48,153
This is the countryside.

106
00:10:51,883 --> 00:10:53,500
Stop working on this case for now.

107
00:10:56,490 --> 00:10:57,546
I'll handle it myself.

108
00:10:59,590 --> 00:11:00,953
I've tried to arrest him before.

109
00:11:02,243 --> 00:11:04,273
But all my colleagues died.

110
00:11:05,216 --> 00:11:06,380
In strange conditions.

111
00:11:07,923 --> 00:11:09,996
Until Itt had to take over
the case himself.

112
00:11:13,063 --> 00:11:14,366
The day Itt disappeared...

113
00:11:15,903 --> 00:11:17,930
Singh was the one who saw something...

114
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:19,790
take his body away.

115
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:22,743
And how long will you keep this hidden?

116
00:11:28,393 --> 00:11:30,016
Until Itt returns.

117
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:32,983
Mr. Itthi is not dead.

118
00:11:34,456 --> 00:11:36,660
So that means you know where he is.

119
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:07,040
So what are you going to do with this sign?

120
00:12:07,506 --> 00:12:07,876
Huh?

121
00:12:08,723 --> 00:12:09,946
Should we just throw it in the sea?

122
00:12:12,446 --> 00:12:13,083
Throw it away.

123
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:14,930
Keep it.

124
00:12:15,916 --> 00:12:17,753
It's still your dream, isn't it?

125
00:12:20,190 --> 00:12:21,340
That terrible dream?

126
00:12:22,823 --> 00:12:23,763
There were good parts too.

127
00:12:26,873 --> 00:12:27,520
That's true.

128
00:12:32,233 --> 00:12:32,923
Well, then I'll...

129
00:12:32,973 --> 00:12:34,216
take it to my mom's house then.

130
00:12:34,990 --> 00:12:36,626
If one day you feel like
opening the shop again,

131
00:12:37,306 --> 00:12:38,153
use the old sign.

132
00:12:38,690 --> 00:12:39,496
It's got good vibes.

133
00:12:43,273 --> 00:12:43,893
And you?

134
00:12:44,653 --> 00:12:45,273
What's next?

135
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:48,783
I'll probably go...

136
00:12:50,593 --> 00:12:52,036
rent out jet skis to tourists...

137
00:12:52,293 --> 00:12:53,016
at the beach.

138
00:12:53,613 --> 00:12:54,966
Or when I'm bored, maybe...

139
00:12:55,416 --> 00:12:56,266
rent out inner tubes.

140
00:12:57,266 --> 00:12:57,960
But if...

141
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,176
you're asking me if I'd sell drugs...

142
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,050
don't even think about it.

143
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:01,926
I'm out.

144
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:06,373
Let's go our separate ways. Go.

145
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:09,373
The contractors will come tomorrow
to clear the stuff out of here.

146
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:11,810
Then...

147
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:14,883
help me take the sign
to your mom's house.

148
00:13:17,966 --> 00:13:18,386
Sure.

149
00:15:33,706 --> 00:15:34,626
And he came alone?

150
00:15:35,470 --> 00:15:36,273
Why bring him here?

151
00:15:39,166 --> 00:15:41,183
To use him as bait, of course.

152
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:43,923
We need big bait.

153
00:15:46,183 --> 00:15:47,733
The big fish will come
for the bait on its own.

154
00:17:03,096 --> 00:17:03,726
Mm-hmm.

155
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:15,673
A decoy, huh?

156
00:17:22,483 --> 00:17:25,493
If you hadn't fallen for it,
I wouldn't be a hitman.

157
00:17:35,796 --> 00:17:38,110
The one who is the Water element,
possesses Water power.

158
00:17:39,346 --> 00:17:41,143
The one whose concentration
is their strength.

159
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:15,280
Only Wind is left.

160
00:18:34,543 --> 00:18:35,100
Hey!

161
00:18:35,663 --> 00:18:36,990
Hey! Fuck!

162
00:18:59,050 --> 00:18:59,816
Give it to me.

163
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:01,800
Singh!

164
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,510
You...

165
00:19:10,756 --> 00:19:12,020
You...

166
00:19:15,646 --> 00:19:16,230
Hey!

167
00:19:16,950 --> 00:19:17,946
I thought you were tough.

168
00:19:18,646 --> 00:19:19,913
You're still just as pathetic as ever.

169
00:19:29,973 --> 00:19:30,586
You bastard!

170
00:19:30,623 --> 00:19:31,123
Damn!

171
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:32,013
Fuck!

172
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:34,273
Damn, get him! Get him!

173
00:19:54,386 --> 00:19:55,796
You fuck! You bastard!

174
00:20:25,443 --> 00:20:27,186
Om, iron flesh, steel tendon.

175
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:30,043
Flesh to flesh, bone to bone.

176
00:20:30,683 --> 00:20:32,766
Tendon to tendon, blood to blood.

177
00:20:32,996 --> 00:20:34,926
Om, join and become one flesh.

178
00:22:24,486 --> 00:22:26,783
The one who is the Wind element,
possesses Wind power.

179
00:22:27,853 --> 00:22:29,630
The one whose concentration
is his strength.

180
00:22:43,490 --> 00:22:44,330
Arise.

181
00:22:46,196 --> 00:22:47,006
Arise.

182
00:22:49,630 --> 00:22:50,576
Arise.

183
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:56,936
You, who are the child of Lord Phaya,
the Wind God.

184
00:22:57,926 --> 00:22:59,536
Merely by the wind's passing,

185
00:23:00,980 --> 00:23:03,273
you shall be revived instantly.

186
00:23:32,916 --> 00:23:33,556
Father.

187
00:24:45,406 --> 00:24:47,036
Finally showing up, damn you.

188
00:24:52,046 --> 00:24:52,926
Do you remember me?

189
00:24:57,610 --> 00:24:58,716
You wicked fuck!

190
00:24:59,346 --> 00:25:01,633
Use your concentration to see who I am!

191
00:25:11,476 --> 00:25:12,940
I had faith.

192
00:25:14,576 --> 00:25:16,566
Faith and respect for you, brother.

193
00:25:21,530 --> 00:25:23,740
That's why I came out
to fight alongside you.

194
00:25:24,706 --> 00:25:26,026
To save our nation.

195
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:30,250
Even death, I do not regret.

196
00:25:31,086 --> 00:25:32,250
And even if I die,

197
00:25:34,430 --> 00:25:37,036
I wish to become a ghost
guarding the town, guarding the nation.

198
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:41,800
To hunt down these wicked,
treacherous scum for all eternity.

199
00:25:51,210 --> 00:25:52,453
They have protective charms.

200
00:25:54,760 --> 00:25:56,226
Those ghost army bastards.

201
00:25:57,736 --> 00:25:58,933
If they use ghosts for protection,

202
00:26:00,040 --> 00:26:01,663
we will use ghosts to kill them.

203
00:26:08,586 --> 00:26:09,940
It's a trap.

204
00:26:48,423 --> 00:26:50,060
Did you think I didn't know?

205
00:26:51,026 --> 00:26:52,023
You have power.

206
00:26:52,750 --> 00:26:53,853
I have power too.

207
00:26:56,186 --> 00:26:57,676
A ghost army like yours...

208
00:26:59,136 --> 00:27:00,703
how resilient can it really be?

209
00:27:04,223 --> 00:27:06,130
I have skilled Khmer masters too.

210
00:27:10,723 --> 00:27:11,576
And you?

211
00:27:12,193 --> 00:27:13,413
Disciples of Master Thammachoti.

212
00:27:29,513 --> 00:27:30,690
There is one more person left.

213
00:27:32,516 --> 00:27:33,690
He's at Bang Rajan.

214
00:27:36,980 --> 00:27:38,573
He wields a pair of axes as weapons.

215
00:28:07,303 --> 00:28:08,696
Do you see that light in the distance?

216
00:28:10,573 --> 00:28:11,970
The fire burning down the whole village.

217
00:28:12,793 --> 00:28:14,350
How beautiful it is.

218
00:28:15,736 --> 00:28:17,373
The villagers' wails...

219
00:28:19,303 --> 00:28:20,330
sound so melodious.

220
00:28:24,093 --> 00:28:25,003
Without you people...

221
00:28:26,253 --> 00:28:27,700
everything would be so much easier.

222
00:28:32,546 --> 00:28:34,336
You are a traitor.

223
00:28:38,110 --> 00:28:40,783
You betrayed this land.

224
00:28:43,776 --> 00:28:45,656
I curse you.

225
00:28:49,283 --> 00:28:51,260
I curse you.

226
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:56,510
I curse you!

227
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:08,546
An ungrateful wretch like you doesn't even
deserve to stand on this land.

228
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:12,080
Betraying.

229
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:13,666
Deceitful.

230
00:29:14,480 --> 00:29:15,150
Fuck you!

231
00:29:16,630 --> 00:29:19,043
You led your comrades to their deaths!
What is your heart made of?

232
00:29:23,013 --> 00:29:24,800
I have already paid my karmic debt.

233
00:29:52,463 --> 00:29:53,813
No need to feel guilty.

234
00:29:57,100 --> 00:30:00,293
It was worth it, trading your life for
the entire village of Bang Rajan.

235
00:30:03,980 --> 00:30:05,046
The Bang Rajan villagers...

236
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,566
cannot withstand our army.

237
00:30:12,653 --> 00:30:14,270
I will ask the general to do you a favor.

238
00:30:36,963 --> 00:30:37,966
Take his body.

239
00:30:39,456 --> 00:30:41,210
Make him a ghost
guarding the various towns.

240
00:30:42,640 --> 00:30:43,133
Yes, sir.

241
00:30:52,686 --> 00:30:53,973
Paid your debt, have you?

242
00:30:54,493 --> 00:30:57,210
Do you know how many days
I was under that log?

243
00:30:58,296 --> 00:30:59,406
I couldn't tell the time anymore!

244
00:31:06,433 --> 00:31:08,783
I lay there watching my own guts spill out.

245
00:31:09,063 --> 00:31:10,353
Day after day!

246
00:31:12,796 --> 00:31:15,093
And I did exactly what you taught me.

247
00:31:17,426 --> 00:31:18,570
I prayed.

248
00:31:19,946 --> 00:31:22,423
I begged for someone, anyone, to help me.

249
00:31:25,823 --> 00:31:26,446
No one.

250
00:31:28,906 --> 00:31:30,360
No one came to help me.

251
00:31:34,176 --> 00:31:35,333
No sacred beings.

252
00:31:38,160 --> 00:31:40,616
No god came to help me.

253
00:31:41,993 --> 00:31:43,976
The reason I'm still here today...

254
00:31:50,026 --> 00:31:52,130
Do you know what I traded for it?

255
00:31:55,690 --> 00:31:57,926
I traded my soul.

256
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:03,030
So I could hunt you down
and have my vengeance

257
00:32:03,060 --> 00:32:04,903
in every life, you bastard, Khong!

258
00:32:09,150 --> 00:32:11,106
You want to be reborn, don't you?

259
00:32:12,653 --> 00:32:13,326
Fine.

260
00:32:15,026 --> 00:32:17,636
I'll make sure you get your rebirth.

261
00:32:19,466 --> 00:32:19,980
You...

262
00:32:21,946 --> 00:32:22,543
Father.

263
00:32:32,023 --> 00:32:33,496
Don't touch my wife and child.

264
00:32:33,703 --> 00:32:34,773
They have nothing to do with this.

265
00:32:39,973 --> 00:32:42,433
And my wife? My family?
Could they beg you for mercy? Huh?!

266
00:32:42,736 --> 00:32:43,460
No!

267
00:32:46,376 --> 00:32:47,180
You are...

268
00:32:47,713 --> 00:32:49,766
being used by evil.

269
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:53,573
If you don't continue the feud...

270
00:32:54,800 --> 00:32:55,970
everything ends.

271
00:32:56,953 --> 00:32:57,693
You end.

272
00:32:58,873 --> 00:32:59,593
I end.

273
00:33:01,196 --> 00:33:02,233
I won't end!

274
00:33:17,326 --> 00:33:17,760
Father.

275
00:33:21,770 --> 00:33:22,240
You fuck!

276
00:33:22,910 --> 00:33:25,816
I will use your very blood to
summon demonic spirits to kill you all!

277
00:33:26,003 --> 00:33:29,103
Even if there are thousands of you,
I will still defeat you!

278
00:33:35,410 --> 00:33:37,360
The one who is the Earth
element, possesses Earth power,

279
00:33:37,406 --> 00:33:39,210
the one whose
concentration is his strength.

280
00:33:48,770 --> 00:33:50,476
The one who is the Fire element,

281
00:33:52,286 --> 00:33:53,500
possesses Fire power.

282
00:33:58,570 --> 00:34:00,423
The one whose concentration
is his strength.

283
00:34:10,073 --> 00:34:10,750
That's it.

284
00:34:51,726 --> 00:34:52,783
Why don't you have your shadow?

285
00:35:06,156 --> 00:35:07,293
He projected his consciousness here.

286
00:35:26,746 --> 00:35:28,296
Fucking piece of shit!

287
00:35:53,096 --> 00:35:53,753
What the hell is this?

288
00:36:20,980 --> 00:36:21,680
Are you okay, Nam?

289
00:36:22,316 --> 00:36:22,940
Not okay.

290
00:36:23,790 --> 00:36:24,883
This time it's really bad.

291
00:36:33,420 --> 00:36:34,063
Hey, wait.

292
00:36:34,383 --> 00:36:35,146
The book.

293
00:36:43,566 --> 00:36:44,473
Where did it go?

294
00:36:47,333 --> 00:36:47,933
Forget it.

295
00:36:48,706 --> 00:36:49,573
It's good that it's gone.

296
00:36:50,940 --> 00:36:52,056
So no one else will suffer because of it.

297
00:36:57,606 --> 00:36:58,040
Let's go.

298
00:37:37,660 --> 00:37:38,066
Master.

299
00:37:40,150 --> 00:37:40,976
What are the lottery numbers for this draw?

300
00:37:42,530 --> 00:37:42,956
Master.

301
00:37:49,740 --> 00:37:50,316
Damn.

302
00:37:51,670 --> 00:37:52,536
Oh no.

303
00:37:53,146 --> 00:37:54,220
That bastard ran away.

304
00:37:54,846 --> 00:37:56,696
- Hey...
- That's not enough.

305
00:38:03,866 --> 00:38:04,996
What are the numbers for this draw, Master?

306
00:38:05,633 --> 00:38:07,123
Give me a good one, Master.
Tell me, Master.

307
00:38:07,360 --> 00:38:08,280
What do you want, Master?

308
00:38:08,510 --> 00:38:09,940
Want some colonel's chicken?
Two drumsticks?

309
00:38:10,086 --> 00:38:10,663
Pizza.

310
00:38:10,713 --> 00:38:12,343
Pickled fruit, fondue, roast pork.

311
00:38:12,526 --> 00:38:14,270
Anything. I can get it all for you, Master.

312
00:38:27,346 --> 00:38:28,480
Someone sent word.

313
00:38:29,406 --> 00:38:31,380
Our team is likely to
be transferred as a whole.

314
00:38:33,036 --> 00:38:34,373
The order will probably come down soon.

315
00:38:35,870 --> 00:38:36,616
I'm sorry.

316
00:38:36,726 --> 00:38:37,603
That you ended up in this team.

317
00:38:38,666 --> 00:38:39,740
I was prepared for it, sir.

318
00:38:40,373 --> 00:38:42,043
Working on cases involving big shots.

319
00:38:44,550 --> 00:38:45,156
Mm-hmm.

320
00:38:49,376 --> 00:38:50,270
Have you noticed, Sergeant?

321
00:38:51,506 --> 00:38:52,743
No matter what we do,

322
00:38:53,650 --> 00:38:55,733
whether it's a suspect or a politician,

323
00:38:56,706 --> 00:38:59,090
they always know everything
one step ahead of us.

324
00:39:00,140 --> 00:39:01,716
Do they have a mole in our team?

325
00:39:07,743 --> 00:39:08,333
Come in.

326
00:39:10,803 --> 00:39:11,970
- Excuse me, sir.
- Mm-hmm.

327
00:39:13,326 --> 00:39:15,220
Urgent dispatch from
the Region 2 Commander, sir.

328
00:39:27,226 --> 00:39:27,746
Huh.

329
00:39:39,586 --> 00:39:41,526
A team member is being omitted
from transferring.

330
00:39:49,630 --> 00:39:50,343
Sarge Ming?

331
00:39:54,286 --> 00:39:54,760
Damn.

332
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:57,850
There are worms everywhere for real.

333
00:40:03,496 --> 00:40:04,860
But the superiors also told me.

334
00:40:06,100 --> 00:40:07,236
We are polices.

335
00:40:08,320 --> 00:40:09,043
Don't lose hope.

336
00:40:11,286 --> 00:40:12,810
Can I tell them back?

337
00:40:13,036 --> 00:40:14,136
They should calm their hands sometimes

338
00:40:14,683 --> 00:40:16,103
on their connections and lobbying.

339
00:40:16,420 --> 00:40:18,550
Be honest about who
they support by connection.

340
00:40:19,016 --> 00:40:21,126
So good doing officers
won't lose their goodwill.

341
00:40:27,903 --> 00:40:29,370
And I still don't know where
will they move us.

342
00:40:30,760 --> 00:40:32,423
I don't know if I'll ever
see our team again.

343
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:37,840
Can I ask you for one thing, Inspector?

344
00:40:39,280 --> 00:40:39,800
What?

345
00:40:42,050 --> 00:40:43,493
Can I call you 'big brother', Inspector?

346
00:40:44,770 --> 00:40:45,226
Hey.

347
00:40:46,306 --> 00:40:46,926
Sure you can.

348
00:40:47,643 --> 00:40:48,813
You can even invite me for a drink.

349
00:40:49,096 --> 00:40:50,046
I'm so stressed out!

350
00:41:11,340 --> 00:41:12,556
So you've decided to go, haven't you?

351
00:41:16,813 --> 00:41:17,606
Want to go together?

352
00:41:23,090 --> 00:41:24,220
But I won't take on jobs.

353
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:27,443
I just want to drive around aimlessly.

354
00:41:29,056 --> 00:41:30,770
I want to forget
everything that's happened.

355
00:41:34,933 --> 00:41:37,133
If you want to run from the truth,
you have to keep running.

356
00:41:38,543 --> 00:41:39,846
Because it will follow you forever.

357
00:41:45,616 --> 00:41:47,080
Just thinking about the past...

358
00:41:50,373 --> 00:41:51,043
Honestly,

359
00:41:51,640 --> 00:41:53,073
when I had amnesia...

360
00:41:53,573 --> 00:41:54,410
it was good in a way.

361
00:41:55,450 --> 00:41:56,713
I forgot so many things.

362
00:42:03,160 --> 00:42:03,800
And...

363
00:42:04,033 --> 00:42:04,770
what about us?

364
00:42:05,240 --> 00:42:05,933
Did you forget that?

365
00:42:14,453 --> 00:42:15,346
I remember.

366
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:17,843
I remember it very well.

367
00:42:22,120 --> 00:42:23,380
The good feelings...

368
00:42:24,600 --> 00:42:25,590
Who could forget those?

369
00:42:27,856 --> 00:42:30,760
Those feelings came
after I lost my memory.

370
00:42:32,753 --> 00:42:33,550
Why are you asking?

371
00:42:35,500 --> 00:42:35,933
I...

372
00:42:37,210 --> 00:42:38,000
I just want to know.

373
00:42:46,340 --> 00:42:47,143
So, what's next?

374
00:42:49,086 --> 00:42:49,740
For me?

375
00:42:51,380 --> 00:42:52,350
I'll stay with Mom.

376
00:42:54,346 --> 00:42:55,666
So I don't have to find
troubles with anyone.

377
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:58,216
Wait for Dad to come back.

378
00:42:59,330 --> 00:43:00,126
And also...

379
00:43:04,270 --> 00:43:05,300
Wait for you to come back, of course.

380
00:43:11,926 --> 00:43:12,953
No need to search.

381
00:43:13,546 --> 00:43:15,156
I'll just stand by and wait here.

382
00:43:18,380 --> 00:43:19,520
The money I have...

383
00:43:20,186 --> 00:43:21,033
I can't spend it all.

384
00:43:22,453 --> 00:43:23,810
Interested in helping me spend it?

385
00:43:30,640 --> 00:43:31,440
As you wish.

386
00:43:45,310 --> 00:43:45,840
Go on.

387
00:44:30,296 --> 00:44:30,793
Mom.

388
00:44:31,010 --> 00:44:33,173
If you let me live here, Mom,
I'm telling you, you'd be comfortable.

389
00:44:33,380 --> 00:44:36,350
- Hmm?
- You just think of me as a servant.

390
00:44:36,546 --> 00:44:38,393
Because in the morning,
I'll have you serve rice.

391
00:44:38,590 --> 00:44:41,096
- At noon, I'll have you serve me laundry.
- Hey, you!

392
00:44:42,473 --> 00:44:44,370
You're nor respecting my age!

393
00:44:44,420 --> 00:44:46,326
A volleyball hit to the face.
Were you a professional, Mom?

394
00:44:47,420 --> 00:44:48,300
Fine, Mom, just think of it as...

395
00:44:48,693 --> 00:44:51,680
me, I'm just another burden for you,
like Fon Fon.

396
00:44:52,853 --> 00:44:53,643
I'll sing a song for you later.

397
00:44:53,890 --> 00:44:54,746
- I'm good at it.
- Jo!

398
00:44:55,660 --> 00:44:56,406
Hey, Singh!

399
00:44:57,233 --> 00:44:58,570
Have some water.
- The table is full of food!

400
00:44:58,653 --> 00:44:59,506
There's even kaprao!

401
00:45:01,310 --> 00:45:02,356
I went all the way to the market.

402
00:45:03,240 --> 00:45:05,876
There are only two of us, Mom.
Why is there so much food?

403
00:45:06,383 --> 00:45:06,696
Huh?

404
00:45:07,073 --> 00:45:08,060
- Hmph.
- Come here.

405
00:45:08,633 --> 00:45:11,536
You really don't keep up
with the world news, do you?

406
00:45:11,563 --> 00:45:12,336
What damn news?

407
00:45:12,443 --> 00:45:13,743
How can you say there are two of us?

408
00:45:14,376 --> 00:45:15,740
There are three of us.

409
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:18,016
Because from now on...

410
00:45:18,283 --> 00:45:19,686
I'll be living in this house.

411
00:45:21,500 --> 00:45:23,010
Don't get too excited. Don't get excited.

412
00:45:23,173 --> 00:45:23,866
I'm used to it.

413
00:45:24,640 --> 00:45:26,243
The reason I'm staying
n this house is because...

414
00:45:26,373 --> 00:45:27,486
food is free.

415
00:45:28,136 --> 00:45:29,046
Bed is free.

416
00:45:29,230 --> 00:45:30,333
Water, electricity, all free.

417
00:45:30,440 --> 00:45:32,396
Free day! Hello! Oh, awesome!

418
00:45:32,440 --> 00:45:33,906
This is my way.

419
00:45:35,176 --> 00:45:35,806
Oh.

420
00:45:36,170 --> 00:45:37,713
Damn you, Jo, you...

421
00:45:39,206 --> 00:45:40,683
I have not a fucking thing
to say other than...

422
00:45:41,500 --> 00:45:43,473
You're truly the most lowlife person
I've ever met.

423
00:45:43,533 --> 00:45:44,896
- Peeling, peeling.
- Thanks for the compliment.

424
00:45:45,236 --> 00:45:46,593
What compliment? I'm cursing you!

425
00:45:46,890 --> 00:45:48,080
- Yeah, Singh.
- Look at this.

426
00:45:48,200 --> 00:45:49,706
Go get my phone for me, son.

427
00:45:49,746 --> 00:45:50,556
I'm too lazy to get up now.

428
00:45:50,913 --> 00:45:52,506
You're quite a handful.

429
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:54,923
- You bastard.
- I'm not competing with you though.

430
00:45:56,033 --> 00:45:57,616
Peel it. Peel, peel, peel.

431
00:45:57,710 --> 00:45:58,866
Tough guy with a cartoon face.

432
00:46:26,673 --> 00:46:28,100
Why did you take so long, Singh?

433
00:46:28,943 --> 00:46:29,633
What's wrong?

434
00:46:30,730 --> 00:46:31,890
Nothing, Mom. It's just...

435
00:46:33,050 --> 00:46:35,303
I don't know where you put it,
so I was looking for a long time.

436
00:46:35,740 --> 00:46:36,170
Oh.

437
00:46:37,166 --> 00:46:37,743
Thanks.

438
00:46:38,273 --> 00:46:39,130
Hey, Singh.

439
00:46:39,826 --> 00:46:42,030
Tomorrow, you have to pick up
Chinese customers for the boat tour, right?

440
00:46:42,523 --> 00:46:43,683
Invite me. I'll go with you.

441
00:46:43,966 --> 00:46:44,470
I like it.

442
00:46:44,510 --> 00:46:45,983
Chinese customers are all so pretty.

443
00:46:46,576 --> 00:46:47,830
If you oversleep, I'll go ahead.

444
00:46:49,213 --> 00:46:51,400
You're going anyway, why be scared?
If I oversleep, just wake me up.

445
00:46:51,480 --> 00:46:53,830
- It's here!
- Wake me up, then.

446
00:46:53,920 --> 00:46:55,546
Grilled shrimp, mantis shrimp, crab.

447
00:46:55,576 --> 00:46:59,550
- Oysters! The specialty is here!
- Oh, wow!

448
00:46:59,586 --> 00:47:00,986
Great job, Foon!

449
00:47:01,020 --> 00:47:02,903
- The table isn't big enough.
- You glutton!

450
00:47:03,186 --> 00:47:05,353
By the time you got here,
I didn't even feel like eating anymore.

451
00:47:05,500 --> 00:47:06,453
Took forever.

452
00:47:08,130 --> 00:47:08,776
You...

453
00:47:09,100 --> 00:47:09,990
You complain so much.

454
00:47:10,040 --> 00:47:12,366
I waited for hours.
Why didn't you help me, huh?

455
00:47:12,533 --> 00:47:14,470
I invited you, but you said
no, said you'd wait here.

456
00:47:14,510 --> 00:47:16,633
You're such a pain, seriously.

457
00:47:16,770 --> 00:47:17,466
You don't have to eat.

458
00:47:17,580 --> 00:47:19,286
Just let Auntie and Singh
eat for the two of us.

459
00:47:19,660 --> 00:47:20,436
Let me eat.

460
00:47:21,600 --> 00:47:22,956
You have such a big mouth.

461
00:47:23,493 --> 00:47:25,043
You shouldn't have even survived.

462
00:47:25,313 --> 00:47:25,896
Damn,

463
00:47:25,920 --> 00:47:26,990
if the Monk Teacher hadn't helped

464
00:47:27,030 --> 00:47:28,800
exorcise the wind possession from you...

465
00:47:29,376 --> 00:47:32,050
I wonder if you'd even be here to sit here
and curse me like this, you bastard.

466
00:47:32,110 --> 00:47:34,246
If I had really died,
I'd have haunted you first.

467
00:47:34,283 --> 00:47:36,106
- Ooh, I'm so scared.
- Are you two going to fight all night?

468
00:47:36,126 --> 00:47:37,776
- Yeah.
- Enough, enough.

469
00:47:37,886 --> 00:47:39,106
- Enough.
- Eat, eat.

470
00:47:39,316 --> 00:47:40,776
- I'm going to throw it all away.
- No, no, no!

471
00:47:40,803 --> 00:47:42,416
- Please don't, Auntie.
- Why are you getting up? Sit down.

472
00:48:08,003 --> 00:48:08,763
Whoo!

473
00:48:30,586 --> 00:48:31,670
Ayutthaya.

474
00:48:32,180 --> 00:48:33,386
Will be mine.

475
00:48:37,913 --> 00:48:39,193
This town will be mine.

476
00:48:39,986 --> 00:48:40,763
All mine.
